1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,333
StudyHub: For HNU FCSIT students: your level’s courses, tasks and archive.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,567
Sign up as an FCSIT student.
Students of the faculty get the archive, college tasks and announcements.

3
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:14,500
Enter the faculty code.
It is shared in your class group.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:20,433
Pick your level and program.
This decides which courses, tasks and announcements you get.

5
00:00:20,567 --> 00:00:23,567
Your overview.
Today’s tasks, your timetable and the latest posts from your class channel.

6
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:27,933
College announcements.
Straight from the WhatsApp channels of your level, through HNU Board.

7
00:00:28,067 --> 00:00:31,733
Step 1: add your courses.
Your courses come from the college archive of your level.

8
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:35,800
The archive opens at your level.
Level 4 · Robotics: this term’s courses with all their lectures.

9
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:39,867
Every lecture is one click away.
PDFs and slides uploaded for the course.

10
00:00:39,967 --> 00:00:48,467
Click Add to my courses.
Do it for every course you are taking this term.

11
00:00:55,567 --> 00:00:57,767
Your courses are ready.
Each one keeps its lectures, tasks, notes and timetable together.

12
00:00:57,867 --> 00:01:01,967
Taking something outside college?
Add it with Course outside college, like a German or ML course.

13
00:01:02,067 --> 00:01:07,333
Step 2: college tasks come by themselves.
Every assignment posted for your level becomes a task, synced every few minutes.

14
00:01:07,433 --> 00:01:11,400
With deadline, course and the post link.
You get reminded 1 day, 12 hours and 1 hour before the deadline.

15
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:17,033
Missed ones show as closed.
They are not counted as your work in the weekly review.

16
00:01:17,133 --> 00:01:22,800
Step 3: bring your Obsidian notes.
Upload your notes folder, or a ZIP of it.

17
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:29,533
Link each course to its notes folder.
Edit the course and pick the folder.

18
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,500
The course page.
Its tasks, college lectures and your notes in one place.

19
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:36,267
College files of the course.
From the archive, always the latest.

20
00:01:36,367 --> 00:01:40,767
Your notes for the course.
Everything from its linked Obsidian folder.

21
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:45,567
Notes look like in Obsidian.
Math, code, callouts, tables and diagrams.

22
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:48,933
Step 4: the AI assistant.
It needs your own free API key the first time.

23
00:01:49,033 --> 00:01:52,000
Get a free key from Groq.
console.groq.com/keys → Create API Key → copy the key starting with gsk_.

24
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:57,167
Paste it and click Save and test.
It is checked, then stored encrypted. Only you use it.

25
00:01:57,267 --> 00:02:00,667
Ask about your lectures.
It searches your notes, reads the right one and tells you which note it used.

26
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,000
Answers from your own notes.
Great for revising before a quiz.

27
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:14,700
It can also add things for you.
Write like you text a friend: quizzes, deadlines, timetable slots.

28
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:24,367
Done, all added.
With deadlines, and linked to the right course.

29
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:28,367
New year or new program?
Change your level here and you get the new courses and tasks.

30
00:02:28,467 --> 00:02:32,600
Weekly review.
Hours studied, time per course and finished tasks.

31
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:36,100
On your phone too.
Open the link and choose Add to Home screen.

32
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:47,400
Happy studying! Website: study-joox-friends.loophole.site · Code: github.com/yousefJooX/studyhub
